  "title": "Shin et al. 2017 (Experiment A) — Open Access Dataset for EEG+NIRS Single-Trial Classification",
  "description": "An open access dataset for hybrid brain-computer interface research combining EEG and near-infrared spectroscopy (NIRS). This portion (Experiment A) contains recordings from 29 healthy participants performing left versus right hand kinesthetic motor imagery over multiple sessions. The data include 30 EEG channels plus EOG, are preprocessed, and are annotated with HED tags. They support single-trial classification and multimodal BCI validation.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 1000 Hz with 30 active electrodes (BrainAmp amplifier, linked-mastoid reference, Fz ground), alongside NIRS recorded at 12.5 Hz (NIRScout). Participants performed 10 s kinesthetic motor imagery of hand opening and closing at a 1 Hz pace after visual arrow cues, with 20 trials per session. Data were re-referenced to a common average, band-pass filtered at 0.5-50 Hz, cleaned of EOG artifacts with ICA, and downsampled to 200 Hz. Baseline classification used CSP, log-variance features, and shrinkage LDA with 10x5-fold cross-validation.",
